Z||000000||Robert||08-10-2000||11:16 PM||||Anyone that is interested in pottery, check out my newest page on my website.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.canterburytrails.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.canterburytrails.com/</A> <P>Last weekend my wife (Meredith, the former potter) and I were evolved in a pit firing at a San Francisco beach.  This was the first time for me; my wife has done a few of these.  It’s not quite done yet; I need to get some studio type pictures of the finished pottery in there.<P>Enjoy<P>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF"> ||||reg||10
Z||000001||tgowens||08-10-2000||11:39 PM||||Robert, that is just too cool -- I wish I could have been there for that - I love things as interesting as making pottery!! -- Soy sauce and Miracle Grow?<P>By the way, it looks like your engine is running just a tad bit rich!<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/WHGD_sig.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||08-10-2000||11:48 PM||||Thanks Terry;  <BR>Our home is filled with pots, sculptures, and artsy things.  Artist love to trade/barter for things.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>You’ll have to check it out when you are back in town. Remember you have a standing invitation for dinner for all the help you’ve given me with computer stuff.<P>Turns out Soy Sauce contains a lot of Salt. Salt and heat produce a red/green color.  Miracle Grow is green to start with, but the results weren't that great.  I think the person who used the Miracle Grow put it on to thick<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||08-11-2000||01:52 AM||||Thanks for the invitation Robert, that means a lot to me -- as for the pottery - I am a Pisces, we are suppossed to be creative -- wonder when creativity is gonna strike ME? - LOL -- not only the computer work and graphics but I was a musician (professionally) for a loooooooong time......<P>Thanks for letting me share in a unique talent of yours and your wife's.<P>(and I still think you need to have your signature looked at - maybe George can fix that)(just teasin' with ya!)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/WHGD_sig.gif">                <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||08-12-2000||10:02 AM||||A real interesting web site, Robert.  The fired pottery was educational.  Now why was the sculptured pottery head the hit of the show?  I looked at the fired image first and thought you had sacrificed someone.<P>Now you have to do a Fiero design pottery for the next firing.  What a bartering product for the Fiero community.  A one of a kind item.||||reg||1
